What is a Data Type?

A data type defines:

What kind of data a variable stores.
What operations can be performed on it.

Example:

age = 21

21 is an integer.

name = "Suman"

"Suman" is a string.

Python Built-in Data Types
Category	Data Types
Numeric	    int, float, complex
Boolean	    bool
Text	    str
Sequence	list, tuple, range
Set	        set, frozenset
Mapping	    dict
Special	    NoneType


